{"type":"new","contents":"import InfoGeometry.Krein.KreinSpace\nimport InfoGeometry.Canonical.Drazin\nimport InfoGeometry.Meta.Architecture\n\n/-!\n# J-self-adjoint projections in Krein spaces\n\nThis module is a thin naming/bridge layer for conductive GraphRAG skeletons.\nThe owner notions already live in `InfoGeometry.Krein.KreinSpace`:\n\n* fundamental symmetry: `KreinSpace.jCLM`;\n* Krein adjoint: `KreinSpace.kreinAdjoint`;\n* Krein/J-self-adjointness: `KreinSpace.IsKreinSelfAdjoint`.\n\nThe bridge deliberately proves only algebraic consequences available from the\ncurrent substrate.  In particular, a J-self-adjoint projection is Drazin\ninvertible because it is idempotent.  It is a Hilbert/star projection only under\nan additional Hilbert self-adjointness hypothesis.\n-/\n\nnamespace InfoGeometry.Krein\n\nopen InfoGeometry.Canonical.Drazin\n\nnamespace KreinSpace\n\nvariable {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H] [CompleteSpace H]\nvariable [KreinSpace H]\n\n/-- GraphRAG-facing alias for the fundamental symmetry as a bounded operator. -/\nnoncomputable abbrev fundamentalSymmetryCLM : H →L[ℝ] H :=\n  jCLM (H := H)\n\n/-- GraphRAG-facing alias for Krein self-adjointness, i.e. `A♯ = A`. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ndef IsJSelfAdjoint (A : H →L[ℝ] H) : Prop :=\n  IsKreinSelfAdjoint (H := H) A\n\n/-- A J-projection is an idempotent operator that is self-adjoint for the Krein adjoint. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\nstructure IsJProjection (P : H →L[ℝ] H) : Prop where\n  idempotent : P * P = P\n  j_self_adjoint : IsJSelfAdjoint (H := H) P\n\n@[simp]\ntheorem isJSelfAdjoint_iff_isKreinSelfAdjoint (A : H →L[ℝ] H) :\n    IsJSelfAdjoint (H := H) A ↔ IsKreinSelfAdjoint (H := H) A := Iff.rfl\n\n/--\nMetric characterization of J-self-adjointness.\n\nThis is the bridge from the GraphRAG phrase \"indefinite inner product\" to the\nrepo owner predicate `IsKreinSelfAdjoint`: `A` is J-self-adjoint iff it is\nsymmetric for `[u,v]_J = ⟪Ju,v⟫`.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem isJSelfAdjoint_iff_kreinInner (A : H →L[ℝ] H) :\n    IsJSelfAdjoint (H := H) A ↔\n      ∀ u v : H, kreinInner (H := H) (A u) v = kreinInner (H := H) u (A v) :=\n  isKreinSelfAdjoint_iff (H := H) A\n\ntheorem IsJProjection.isJSelfAdjoint {P : H →L[ℝ] H}\n    (hP : IsJProjection (H := H) P) :\n    IsJSelfAdjoint (H := H) P :=\n  hP.j_self_adjoint\n\n/--\nA J-projection is its own Drazin inverse at index `1`.\n\nThis is an algebraic consequence of idempotence; no spectral contour or\nFredholm statement is being asserted.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem IsJProjection.isDrazinInverse_self {P : H →L[ℝ] H}\n    (hP : IsJProjection (H := H) P) :\n    IsDrazinInverse P P 1 :=\n  IsDrazinInverse.of_idempotent hP.idempotent\n\n/-- The Drazin projector of a J-projection with inverse `P` is definitionally `P * P`. -/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem IsJProjection.drazinProjection_eq_self {P : H →L[ℝ] H}\n    (hP : IsJProjection (H := H) P) :\n    IsDrazinInverse.projection P P = P := by\n  simpa [IsDrazinInverse.projection] using hP.idempotent\n\n/--\nIf a J-projection is also Hilbert self-adjoint, then its Drazin projector is a\nstar projection.\n\nThe extra Hilbert self-adjointness hypothesis is real: Krein/J-self-adjointness\nalone does not generally imply Hilbert self-adjointness.\n-/\n@[rep_depth krein]\ntheorem IsJProjection.drazinProjection_isStarProjection_of_hilbertSelfAdjoint\n    {P : H →L[ℝ] H}\n    (hP : IsJProjection (H := H) P)\n    (hHilbert : star P = P) :\n    IsStarProjection (IsDrazinInverse.projection P P) :=\n  IsDrazinInverse.projection_isStarProjection_of_selfAdjoint\n    (hP.isDrazinInverse_self) hHilbert\n\nend KreinSpace\n\nend InfoGeometry.Krein\n","mtime":1778215426031}